QA3 C2. A tracked wrapper overwritten whole with a copy of another (*p = *q):
the copy is a later writer of every field, which stores what that field of *q
holds. ErrClosed, which only the copied value holds, is reported "via field";
ErrExist, held by a wrapper that is never copied, is not. (The copy reads the
field it writes, a cycle of stores: hence the second, "chain may repeat"
entry.)
-- args --
a.go:@q
